meta {
  name: Notes
  seq: 8
}

docs {
  # Notes and highlights

  Private notes about a book. `kind` is fixed at creation: a `note` is the reader's own
  Markdown text (up to 20,000 characters) and a `highlight` is a plain-text quotation (up to
  5,000 characters) with optional Markdown `commentary`. Either may carry a `title`, a free-text
  `chapter` label and a `pageNumber`, and may be linked to one reading session of the same book.
  The API stores and returns the text verbatim (only surrounding whitespace is trimmed) and never
  renders it; a client must render Markdown safely and must not trust embedded HTML.

  Run the folder in order. **Register notes reader** creates its own disposable account, and the
  folder creates its own books and reading session, so it is independent of every other folder.
  Contract: `docs/api-contract.md` ("Notes and highlights").
}
